  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A positive integer N≥1N\\ge 1N≥1 is given.\nAn NNN-uple (x1,x2,…,xN)(x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_N)(x1​,x2​,…,xN​) of nonnegative integers is special if, after we remove all entries which are zero, its entries are nondecreasing. For example (0,2,0,0,4,0,4,5,0,0)(0, 2, 0, 0, 4, 0, 4, 5, 0, 0)(0,2,0,0,4,0,4,5,0,0) is special, but (3,2,0)(3, 2, 0)(3,2,0) and (0,1,3,0,0,1,0)(0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 1, 0)(0,1,3,0,0,1,0) are not.\n\nOne can show that there is a unique function μ\\muμ defined on the NNN-uples of nonnegative integers such that, for any NNN-uple x=(x1,x2,…,xN)x=(x_1, x_2,\\dots, x_N)x=(x1​,x2​,…,xN​)\n\n∑y≤xμ(y)={1if&nbsp;x&nbsp;is&nbsp;special0otherwise,\\sum_{y \\le x} \\mu(y) =\n\\begin{cases}\n    1 &amp;\\text{if $x$ is special} \\\\\n    0 &amp;\\text{otherwise}\n\\end{cases},y≤x∑​μ(y)={10​if&nbsp;x&nbsp;is&nbsp;specialotherwise​,where the sum ranges over all NNN-uples y=(y1,y2,…,yN)y=(y_1, y_2,\\dots, y_N)y=(y1​,y2​,…,yN​) of nonnegative integers such that yi≤xiy_i\\le x_iyi​≤xi​ for all 1≤i≤N1\\le i\\le N1≤i≤N.\n\nYou are given N,M≥1N, M \\ge 1N,M≥1. Compute the remainder modulo 998 244 353998\\,244\\,353998244353 of the number of NNN-uples x=(x1,x2,…,xN)x=(x_1,x_2,\\dots, x_N)x=(x1​,x2​,…,xN​) such that 0≤xi≤M0\\le x_i\\le M0≤xi​≤M for all 1≤i≤N1\\le i\\le N1≤i≤N and μ(x)=0\\mu(x) = 0μ(x)=0.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe only line contains two positive integers NNN, MMM, the size of the tuples and the maximum possible value of the entries of the tuples.\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint the the number of NNN-uples x=(x1,x2,…,xN)x=(x_1,x_2,\\dots, x_N)x=(x1​,x2​,…,xN​) such that 0≤xi≤M0\\le x_i\\le M0≤xi​≤M for all 1≤i≤N1\\le i\\le N1≤i≤N and μ(x)=0\\mu(x) = 0μ(x)=0. As it can be large, print it modulo 998 244 353998\\,244\\,353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤1001 \\leq N \\leq 1001≤N≤100",
      "1≤M≤1001 \\leq M \\leq 1001≤M≤100"
    ],
